cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AxolotlDB in research, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "AxolotlDB: a from-scratch relational and vector database engine as a testbed for database research"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Youssef
    family-names: Ben Youssef
repository-code: "https://github.com/youssefbenyoussefyby/Axolotl"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
date-released: 2026-02-03
keywords:
  - database systems
  - query processing
  - query optimization
  - vector search
  - semantic operators
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  AxolotlDB is a relational and vector database engine written from scratch in
  C++20: paged storage, buffer pool, SQL front end, logical and physical
  planning, and a Volcano-style executor. Every layer is owned and tested, so it
  serves as a controlled testbed for language-model-aware database features:
  semantic filters over text columns, model-assisted query optimization, and
  memory-like storage with semantic compression.
